 Question

   In alignment with security compliance standards, the Nautilus project team has opted to impose restrictions on crontab access. Specifically, only designated users will be permitted to create or update cron jobs.
Configure crontab access on App Server 2 as follows: Allow crontab access to james user while denying access to the jerome user.

            Solution
1-Login into app server2
   ssh steve@stapp02
2-Allow james to use crontab
   echo "james" | sudo tee -a /etc/cron.allow
3-Deny jerome from using crontab
   echo "jerome" | sudo tee -a /etc/cron.deny
4-Verify configuration
  Check the contents of both files:
   cat /etc/cron.allow
   cat /etc/cron.deny
  Expected output:
   # /etc/cron.allow
   james
   # /etc/cron.deny
   jerome

